# Inspection pin

The Platinum prototype is a CDP client of the Servo fork. It does not pin a
Chrome revision and it does not load the Chrome DevTools frontend.

Ordinary browsing uses an in-process client (`cdp_builtin_enabled`). That
does not open a socket. An external listener is a separate development
option: `cdp_server_enabled` plus a non-empty `cdp_server_token`. The
listener accepts only a loopback `Host`, an empty or devtools `Origin`, and
a matching `token` query parameter. `/json/list` advertises
`ws://127.0.0.1:<port>/devtools/page/<id>?token=<token>`.

WebMCP page API: `document.modelContext`, Community Group draft of 27 October
2026. It is behind `dom_webmcp_enabled` (default off) and `[SecureContext]`.
Registration takes a tool dictionary. `execute` returns a promise. The
inspection channel still carries JSON strings; the page and CDP boundaries
convert them. Declarative form attributes are not implemented.

`WebMCP.invokeTool` takes `toolName`, optional `frameId`, and an `input`
object. `toolsAdded` reports `inputSchema` as an object. `toolsRemoved`
reports `{ tools: [{ name, frameId }] }`. `toolResponded` reports `status`
(`success`, `error`, or `cancelled`), `output`, and `errorText`.

Inspection follows the top-level document of the tab on screen. A child
frame does not replace that document. A Start tab or native search results
detach, even if the tab still stores an older page.

The prototype sends these methods. The server answers anything else with
JSON-RPC -32601.

- Runtime.enable
- Runtime.evaluate
- Log.enable
- Page.enable
- Page.getFrameTree
- DOM.enable
- DOM.getDocument
- DOM.requestChildNodes
- DOM.setAttributeValue
- CSS.enable
- CSS.getComputedStyleForNode
- Overlay.enable
- Overlay.highlightNode
- Network.enable
- Network.getResponseBody
- WebMCP.enable
- WebMCP.invokeTool

Events the prototype shows: `Log.entryAdded`, `Runtime.executionContextCreated`,
`Runtime.executionContextDestroyed`, `DOM.setChildNodes`,
`Network.requestWillBeSent`, `Network.responseReceived`,
`Network.loadingFailed`, `WebMCP.toolsAdded`, `WebMCP.toolsRemoved`,
`WebMCP.toolResponded`.
